{"skill":{"slug":"google-calendar-scheduling","displayName":"Google Calendar"},"version":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1782207854741,"changelog":"Rename display name to Google Calendar (published under correct hith3sh account)","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":15488,"sha256":"6334b16559bb255168dd117606dd04c39e3255d1dd45c1351a63b0ab16f7cadc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2538,"sha256":"de8321667990c918f6cc4c0ffad8ba27c9a2dda6a37547f0e5c92d8be15c1a92","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789546360996,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"65328997fef2fb3963fb2555d6ea034ad97b0218ebee396a6957747a8d03f953","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/65328997fef2fb3963fb2555d6ea034ad97b0218ebee396a6957747a8d03f953","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1782211910776},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":8,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789546360996},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Google Calendar skill is mostly coherent, but it should be reviewed because it installs and allowlists an unpinned third-party plugin that handles OAuth-backed calendar access.","dimensions":[{"detail":"OAuth token handling through ClawLink and access to calendars available to the connected Google account are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but the resulting authority includes sensitive reads and writes across calendar data.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install instructions add `clawhub:clawlink-plugin` without a pinned version, digest, or in-artifact verification step, then allowlist the plugin and restart the gateway, making the reviewed skill depend on mutable external plugin code.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill repeatedly instructs the agent to preview and get explicit user confirmation before write, destructive, move, or delete actions, which addresses the high-impact calendar operations.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The setup persistently modifies OpenClaw configuration by adding the plugin to `tools.alsoAllow` and restarting the gateway; removal, rollback, and token revocation guidance are not provided in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Google Calendar scheduling, and the documented capabilities match that purpose, including listing calendars, finding free time, creating events, deleting events, and managing calendar access rules.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review the ClawLink plugin source, publisher, version, and verification status before installing. Use the smallest practical Google Calendar permission scope, confirm every calendar write or sharing change, and know how to remove the plugin and revoke the OAuth connection if needed.","findings":"[EA2] expected: The cited behavior is that Google Calendar sends invitations when creating events with attendees; the artifact also says writes, moves, deletes, and destructive actions require preview and explicit confirmation, so this is disclosed integration behavior rather than unsupported autonomous execution.\n[T08] expected: Installing ClawLink is necessary for this skill's integration model, but the artifact-backed concern remains because the plugin install is unpinned and then granted tool access for OAuth-backed calendar operations.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789546360996}}}}}